# Copy this file to .env (gitignored; chmod 600 .env) and fill it in; every script and the notebook read .env
# automatically, and its values win over variables exported in the shell. The notebook can also do this for you:
# its first cell tests a pasted key against the endpoint and saves it here once, and asks for the judge model.

# 1. Create an API key in Cynos, https://app.cynos.averlon.ai (it starts with sk-cy-). Required.
CYNOS_API_KEY=sk-cy-...

# 2. The judge model for stage 2 (judge.py and the notebook), served on the same endpoint. Required.
AVN_JUDGE_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017

# Optional: a different endpoint (default https://api.cynos.averlon.ai/v1)
# AVN_BASE_URL=https://api.cynos.averlon.ai/v1
